1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,020
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:04,360
and the X-ray keeps
coming back fine,

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,480
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:07,990
I've been
grooming dogs

5
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:09,320
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,690
Kneeling on
the floor

7
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:11,940
and lifting
dogs onto

8
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,660
the table all day.

9
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:14,590
I had my right knee

10
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,290
replaced two
years ago.

11
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:18,300
It has hurt every
day since.

12
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:20,520
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,660
I know what
that felt like,

14
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:22,920
and it went away.

15
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,160
This is different.

16
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,060
Tight.

17
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,070
Full.

18
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:27,340
Like a band
around the joint

19
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,820
that never loosens.

20
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:29,910
And for two
years I've

21
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:31,570
been told the
same thing.

22
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:32,600
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,370
At six weeks it
was swelling,

24
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:35,780
and swelling
is normal.

25
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:38,610
At three months,
give it six.

26
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:39,630
At six months,

27
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:41,340
some knees take
a full year.

28
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:42,220
At a year,

29
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:44,240
eighteen months
isn't unusual.

30
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,710
And I didn't
just wait.

31
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:47,220
We went down
the list.

32
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,790
More physical
therapy.

33
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:52,060
Every session, every
exercise at home.

34
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,190
I got stronger.

35
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:54,890
The tightness
never moved.

36
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:56,180
The pain pills
helped,

37
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:57,640
and that was
the problem.

38
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,730
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:00,800
and nobody
could tell me

40
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,040
when I'd get
to stop.

41
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,720
Then a nerve block.

42
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:06,670
Then talk of burning
the nerve.

43
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:07,720
And after that,

44
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:09,640
a second operation
to go back

45
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,390
in and do it over.

46
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:12,480
I said no.

47
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,730
Every morning I
stepped out of bed

48
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:15,680
and my knee felt

49
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,670
like a band was
wrapped around it,

50
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:20,300
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

51
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,970
Every morning I took
something for it

52
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:23,490
and opened
up the shop.

53
00:01:23,490 --> 00:01:24,900
Couldn't do
the stairs,

54
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,920
couldn't kneel to
clip a dog's nails,

55
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,440
couldn't stand at the
counter long enough

56
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,480
to finish dinner,

57
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,100
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,980
without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,430
It woke me at night,

60
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:36,450
and it turned
ordinary things,

61
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:37,800
like getting
in the car

62
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,180
or up off the couch,

63
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,450
into a decision.

64
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:42,520
Some days I
had to ask

65
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,460
for help
getting a big

66
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,000
dog up on the table.

67
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,590
After a long and
serious talk

68
00:01:46,590 --> 00:01:47,970
with my husband,
I went back

69
00:01:47,970 --> 00:01:49,490
in one more time.

70
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:50,600
That was the
fourth set

71
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,250
of X-rays on
this knee.

72
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,140
And like the
three before it,

73
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:57,240
the answer was
everything looks great.

74
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,700
No loosening, no infection,
nothing wrong.

75
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:01,810
Only this time there

76
00:02:01,810 --> 00:02:03,040
was no new number.

77
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:05,940
Nobody said give it
another six months.

78
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:06,740
There was
nothing left

79
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:07,770
to give it.

80
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:08,940
I sat in the
parking lot

81
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:10,010
for a while.

82
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:11,900
Okay, I thought.

83
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,350
Then explain this.

84
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:16,300
Anyway, a couple
of months back,

85
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,740
I hit my
breaking point.

86
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:18,910
It was around 2:30

87
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,770
in the morning.

88
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:20,830
I had six dogs

89
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:22,210
booked the
next morning.

90
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:24,060
Everyone in the
house was asleep

91
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,030
and I was
downstairs

92
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:25,660
in the recliner

93
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,820
with my leg up,

94
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,820
trying to find any

95
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:28,850
angle where
it didn't feel

96
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:30,060
like something was
wrapped around

97
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,590
my knee and
tightening.

98
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,850
My husband didn't know
I'd come downstairs.

99
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:36,030
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

100
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,580
And I just thought,

101
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:39,440
is this really
my life now?

102
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,070
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:42,330
Thirty years,

104
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,340
and I didn't know
how many

105
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,880
more dogs I
had in me.

106
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,870
So I made myself
a promise.

107
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:48,580
I wouldn't go a day
without looking

108
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:49,590
for an answer.

109
00:02:49,590 --> 00:02:50,900
And when I
found one,

110
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,240
I'd share it

111
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,500
with everyone going
through the same thing.

112
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,570
So I got my
laptop out

113
00:02:56,570 --> 00:02:57,640
and went looking.

114
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:59,690
Not for a product.

115
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:01,360
For an explanation.

116
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,170
Mayo Clinic forums,

117
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:05,300
the knee replacement
group on Facebook,

118
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,370
doctor videos,
medical animations.

119
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:09,720
And that's when
I found a video

120
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,680
from a physical
therapist named Dr.

121
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,750
Steven Salinger,
whose own wife

122
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,530
had been through
exactly this.

123
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,070
But before I say
anything else,

124
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:18,760
I want to be
straight with you.

125
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,440
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,290
The ice.

127
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:25,080
The first week
of a new pill.

128
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,300
The good day
after a session.

129
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,510
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:30,650
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:32,650
Fast relief
isn't relief.

132
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:34,250
It's a preview.

133
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:34,940
So I'm not going

134
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:36,660
to tell you this
works fast.

135
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:37,640
It doesn't.

136
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,480
But if you're willing

137
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,430
to be patient,

138
00:03:39,430 --> 00:03:40,200
and to look
at what's

139
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,200
going on around
your new

140
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,180
knee instead
of inside it,

141
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:43,830
there is a real

142
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:45,540
reason it still hurts.

143
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:47,630
And something you
can do about it.

144
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:49,200
Let me explain
what he said,

145
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,020
because this is what
changed everything

146
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:51,760
for me.

147
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,540
He started with
the basics.

148
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,450
A knee replacement
takes out the

149
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:57,230
worn joint surfaces
and puts

150
00:03:57,230 --> 00:03:58,710
in metal and plastic.

151
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,520
That's what stops
the arthritis pain

152
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,400
you had before
the operation.

153
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,150
That part I
already knew.

154
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,460
But then he explained
something

155
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:07,060
nobody had
ever told me.

156
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:08,400
He said, think
about a

157
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,300
swollen foot
inside a shoe.

158
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,710
The shoe
didn't shrink.

159
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,700
Your foot is taking
up more room,

160
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,130
so everything
feels cramped

161
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:16,770
and tight and
squeezed.

162
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:17,820
Your new knee sits

163
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,840
in a limited space

164
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,220
with living tissue
packed all around it.

165
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,750
To put that knee in,

166
00:04:22,750 --> 00:04:23,480
the surgeon had

167
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,190
to work through
that tissue.

168
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:27,900
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,180
At first that's
normal.

170
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:31,480
But in some people

171
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,990
that swelling can
stay switched

172
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:34,970
on far longer
than expected.

173
00:04:34,970 --> 00:04:36,770
And swollen tissue
takes up more

174
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:38,650
room than calm
tissue does.

175
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:40,380
So when you bend,

176
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,300
that tissue gets
compressed.

177
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,240
When you
straighten,

178
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,740
it gets pulled tight.

179
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:45,840
That's the band.

180
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:46,650
That's the ache

181
00:04:46,650 --> 00:04:48,440
that never
quite leaves.

182
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,210
And you start being

183
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:50,330
the one who says,

184
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:51,280
you go ahead.

185
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,380
I'll stay here.

186
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:53,510
And that's
exactly why

187
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:54,300
so much of what

188
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,010
I'd tried hadn't
worked.

189
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:57,420
Physical therapy
strengthens the

190
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:58,730
muscles around
the knee.

191
00:04:58,730 --> 00:05:00,860
Worth doing,
and I'd done it.

192
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:01,760
It does nothing
about

193
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,260
tissue taking
up room.

194
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,520
A nerve block
quiets the

195
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,580
nerve carrying
the signal.

196
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,680
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

197
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:09,680
But when

198
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,170
that irritated tissue
finally calms down,

199
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:13,590
it holds less fluid,

200
00:05:13,590 --> 00:05:15,270
and it takes up
less room.

201
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:16,530
Less room taken
up means

202
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:18,610
less pressure
squeezing the joint.

203
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:20,470
That's what takes
the pressure off.

204
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:22,060
After two
years of this,

205
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,600
it finally
made sense.

206
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:26,180
The problem was
never the new knee.

207
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,120
It was the tissue
crowded around it.

208
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,700
He calls it the
squeeze.

209
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:30,840
Once you've felt it,

210
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,980
that's the word.

211
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,370
I'd bought
knee sleeves,

212
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:34,680
a foam
kneeling pad,

213
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,740
compression
braces, creams,

214
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:38,280
half of Amazon
really,

215
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,280
and all any of it

216
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,940
gave me was
an hour.

217
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,820
I even looked
at going

218
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:43,350
to a clinic

219
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:44,510
for the light
therapy.

220
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:46,570
But at $200
a session

221
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:48,490
with nothing covered
by insurance,

222
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:49,920
that was a quick no.

223
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,680
Then one night
I went back

224
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,290
to that knee
replacement group

225
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:54,630
and actually read it.

226
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:56,160
Thousands
of people,

227
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:57,780
years out from
surgery,

228
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,210
comparing notes
on stiffness

229
00:05:59,210 --> 00:06:01,520
and tightness nobody
could explain.

230
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:03,920
And no matter how
far I scrolled,

231
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,770
the same thing
kept coming up.

232
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:07,280
This one device,

233
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,160
and people saying it

234
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:08,950
was the first thing

235
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:10,220
that made a
difference.

236
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:12,220
And before anyone
jumps in thinking,

237
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:13,860
alright, here
it comes,

238
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,140
she's selling me
something,

239
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:15,640
let me shut

240
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,960
that down
right now.

241
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,040
I'm only here
because I made

242
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,420
myself a promise
at 2:30

243
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,350
in the morning that

244
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,420
if I ever found
something

245
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:24,130
that helped,
I'd say so.

246
00:06:24,130 --> 00:06:25,360
It's called the
KenRelief

247
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,260
Red Light
Therapy Wrap.

248
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:29,650
At first glance I
didn't buy it.

249
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:30,340
It looked like the

250
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,180
cheap knee sleeves
off Amazon

251
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,780
that did nothing
for me.

252
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:34,150
But I went

253
00:06:34,150 --> 00:06:35,610
to their website
anyway,

254
00:06:35,610 --> 00:06:36,290
just to see what

255
00:06:36,290 --> 00:06:37,780
all the fuss
was about.

256
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:39,280
It's the same red
light therapy

257
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,490
clinics charge $200
a session for,

258
00:06:42,490 --> 00:06:45,230
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

259
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:46,270
in a wrap you plug

260
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:47,800
into the wall
at home.

261
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:49,910
Two hundred and
forty lights.

262
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,200
Red at 660
nanometers

263
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,770
and near-infrared
at 850,

264
00:06:54,770 --> 00:06:57,210
run together for the
strongest effect.

265
00:06:57,210 --> 00:06:59,130
Four strength
levels.

266
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:01,140
A five to thirty
minute timer.

267
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:02,900
Then I saw the
guarantee.

268
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:04,080
Ninety days.

269
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,900
Results or your
money back,

270
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,380
no questions, no
store credit,

271
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:10,120
and you don't even
send it back.

272
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,290
No physical
therapist ever

273
00:07:12,290 --> 00:07:13,360
gave me
ninety days

274
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,750
to change my mind.

275
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:16,250
There wasn't
much to lose,

276
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,350
so I ordered it.

277
00:07:17,350 --> 00:07:18,820
Two of them,
actually.

278
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,500
Only the right knee
was replaced,

279
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:22,230
but you favor the
leg that hurts,

280
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:22,790
and I'd done it

281
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:23,940
for two years.

282
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:25,810
The left one was carrying
the difference.

283
00:07:25,810 --> 00:07:26,740
When it came,

284
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:28,510
I strapped it on
expecting nothing,

285
00:07:28,510 --> 00:07:29,710
because I'd been
let down too

286
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:31,440
